  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nWV imagery indicates a northwest flow aloft prevailing across the \nWestern High Plains downstream of a ridge centered across the Desert \nSouthwest. Near the surface, a lee side trough of low pressure is \nslowly strengthening across eastern Colorado.\n\nMinimal thunderstorm chances (20%) exist across west central/central \nKansas this evening as the SREF indicates a weak upper level \nshortwave and associated H5 vort maxima cycling southeast off the \nridge axis in the Northern Rockies into the high plains of western \nNebraska and northeast Colorado. Near the surface, prevailing \nsoutherlies will support pooling moisture ahead of an advancing \ndryline, providing modest instability with MUCAPE values upward of \n1000 J/kg or so. Despite weaker dynamic support aloft, steeping mid-\nlevel lapse rates in vicinity of an axis of increased low level \nconvergence associated with the dryline will set the stage for \npotential isolated thunderstorm development this evening as H5 vort \nmaxima transition through. This is suggested by a few CAMs and the \nHREF pointing to only a 10 to 20% probability of 6-hr QPF exceeding \na mere 0.1 of an inch in vicinity of the I-70 corridor by late \nevening. Hotter/drier conditions are likely the next couple of days \nas southwesterly downsloping enhances a drier air mass across the \nWestern High Plains.\n\nVery warm temperatures are forecast tonight as southwesterly \ndownsloping reinforces a warmer air mass across southwest/central \nKansas. With the HREF painting a 70-90% probability of temperatures \ndropping below 75F in west central and extreme southwest Kansas to \nto only a 10-20% probability of slipping below 75F in south central \nKansas, look for lows generally down into 70s(F). Southwesterly \ndownsloping will further enhance drier air into southwest Kansas \nSunday, nudging H85 temperatures up from Saturday with a little \nabove 30C in central Kansas to near 35C near the Colorado line. \nExpect widespread afternoon highs topping 100F with the HREF showing \na widespread 80-90% probability of temperatures exceeding the \ncentury mark. Similar conditions are likely Monday.",
